# gr-L1-requirements-quality-gate — LLM-Driven Colang Implementation
# Layer: L1 — fires at L1-requirements-elicitor-evaluator's post_execution
# Validates L1-requirements-elicitor's RESULTANT output (not the evaluator's own bookkeeping)
# Python actions preserved in actions.py for reference/hybrid mode

define flow check output requirements quality gate
  """LLM validates L1-requirements-elicitor's resultant output against its own schema and ISO/IEC/IEEE 29148 rubric."""
  $result = execute self_check_output

  if not $result
    bot block requirements quality gate violation
    stop

define bot block requirements quality gate violation
  "L1-requirements-elicitor's resultant output (post-evaluation) failed its quality gate: schema violation, an ID gap, a broken compound-split reference, or an unqualified vague term detected. The workflow cannot proceed to nfr-classifier/prd-composer with non-conformant requirements. Retrying."
